  "title": "SpaceX's Crew-13 Launches to International Space Station",
  "summary": "NASA’s SpaceX Crew-13 mission launched successfully, with four astronauts aboard the International Space Station, marking a continuation of their mission into spring. The crew includes a Canadian astronaut whose wife will give birth while they are away.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "NASA’s SpaceX Crew-13 mission launched successfully on Thursday at 11:10 a.m. EDT from Space Launch Complex 40 at Cape Canaveral Space Force Station in Florida.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The crew, including a Canadian astronaut, will conduct a science expedition aboard the International Space Station, with the mission scheduled to continue into spring.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The launch was delayed due to a leaking fuel system, but the skies cleared enough for a safe liftoff.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
